The documentation website's admission animation bundles three.js 0.186.1: MIT;
LICENSES/three-MIT.txt (also served as docs/site/three-LICENSE.txt). It is part of
the website only, not of the executable.

Bundled third-party materials in the default release:

- Rust crates linked into the executable (sqlx with SQLite, tokio, rustls with
  ring and the system trust store, and their dependencies): each under its own
  permissive license (MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD-3-Clause, Zlib, Unicode-3.0 or
  Unlicense). The complete list of crates, versions and licenses for a release
  is in LICENSES/THIRD-PARTY-RUST.txt, generated with `cargo xtask licenses`.
- SQLite: public domain; sqlite.org/copyright.html. Compiled from the
  amalgamation bundled by libsqlite3-sys.
- daisyUI and Tailwind CSS: MIT; LICENSES/daisyUI-MIT.txt and
  LICENSES/Tailwind-MIT.txt. Only the generated console stylesheet is bundled;
  Node and npm are not build or runtime dependencies.
- Natural Earth 5.1.2 country boundaries: public domain. The console's world
  geometry is derived from ne_110m_admin_0_countries (see
  cmd/console-ui/web/assets/GEOGRAPHY.md).
- musl libc (statically linked Linux release binaries only): MIT;
  LICENSES/musl-COPYRIGHT.txt.

GeoIP datasets are not bundled. An operator imports one at run time; the
default provider, ip-location-db user-country, is PDDL 1.0, and DB-IP IP to
Country Lite is CC BY 4.0.
